From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:05:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/40] chore: remove resident_static_before_animated (dead
 after ARGB4444 plane bake)

The ARGB4444/PALPHA plane bake (Task 5/6, host-side only -- not part of this
patch series) gives every baked plane real per-pixel alpha, so its one-shot
full-frame COPY is safe to fire wherever the per-bucket static-replay path
already fires (after animated ops, patch 0031) on every layer -- including
the base layer. That made Renderer::resident_static_before_animated() (added
by patch 0032, needed by the old base-layer-only opaque-COPY design)
permanently return false from every override, and the _static_first branch
in Entities::draw() dead. Delete the base virtual and restore the
unconditional animated-then-static order patch 0031 established.
---
 include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h | 12 ------------
 src/entities/Entities.cpp           | 22 +++++++++-------------
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h b/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
index a34059f..de99329 100644
--- a/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
+++ b/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
@@ -125,18 +125,6 @@ public:
   // renderer with no plane support (or the default no-op Renderer) simply draws
   // nothing here, matching the old per-op accessors' zero-count default.
   virtual void resident_emit_static_layer(int /*layer*/) {}
-  // [Phase 3b] Where does resident_emit_static_layer belong relative to this layer's
-  // animated op loop? A per-op static replay (the common case) only ever contains
-  // tiles that don't overlap any animated tile's square, so it's order-independent
-  // and the engine puts it AFTER (false here) so animated content -- including a
-  // scroll_ratio!=1 background pattern -- isn't hidden behind ground it should show
-  // through. A single-plane bake that flattens EVERY layer's statics into one image
-  // and fires its one-shot full-frame COPY on whichever layer is drawn first (see
-  // MisterBlitterRenderer::resident_emit_static_layer) instead needs to run BEFORE
-  // any animated/entity draws of ANY layer this frame, exactly like it always did --
-  // otherwise that opaque COPY wipes out the first layer's own just-drawn animated
-  // tiles. Override to return true while such a plane is active.
-  virtual bool resident_static_before_animated(int /*layer*/) const { return false; }
 
   /**
    * @brief clear a surface
